    "text": "D. Upon the discovery of a “pollution condition’, the “insured” shall make every attempt to mitigate any loss and comply with applicable “environmental law\". The Insurer shall have the right, but not the duty, to mitigate such “pollution conditions” if, in the sole judgment of the insurer, the “insured” fails to take reasonable steps to do so. _ In that event, any \"remediation costs” incurred by the Insurer shall be deemed incurred by the “insured”, and shall be subject to the “self-insured retention” and Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy."
