    "text": "Fungi and Legionella “Claims”, “remediation costs” or “legal defense expenses” arising out of or related to the actual, alleged, or threatened inhalation of, ingestion of, contact with, exposure to, existence of, or presence of, any “fungi”, fegionella pneumophila, or odor regardless of whether any other cause, event, material, or product contributed concurrently or in any sequence to such injury or damage. This exclusion shall also apply to any costs or expense arising out of or related to the testing for, monitoring, cleaning up, removing, containing, treating, detoxifying, neutralizing, remediating, or disposing of, or in any way responding to or assessing the effects of, “fungi’, fegionella pneumophila, or odor by any “insured” or by any other person or entity."
  },
  {
    "id": "c181",
    "name": "Endorsement 12 — Natural Resource Damage Sublimit",
    "text": "Hl. $500,000 shall be the Aggregate Sublimit of Liability for “claims” for “natural resource damage” for which coverage exists under this Policy. Therefore, this Aggregate Sublimit of Liability shall be the maximum amount the insurer shall pay for all “claims” and associated “legal defense expenses” arising out of “natural resource damage”. This Aggregate Sublimit of Liability shall be subject to the Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy. Under no circumstance shail the Insurer be liable to pay any amount in excess of any applicable Limit of Liability."
  },
  {
    "id": "c182",
    "name": "Endorsement 12 — Unchanged Terms",
    "text": "All other terms and conditions of this Policy remain unchanged."
  },
  {
    "id": "c183",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Products Pollution Coverage",
    "text": "SUPPLEMENTAL COVERAGE — PRODUCTS POLLUTION “Claims” and associated “legal defense expense”, in excess of the “self insured retention”, arising out of “product pollution\", provided that the “claim” is first made during the “policy period”. Any such “claim” must be reported to the Insurer, in writing, during the “policy period” or any applicable “extended reporting period”,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c184",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Products Pollution Timing",
    "text": "The coverage afforded pursuant to this Supplemental Coverage only applies to “product pollution” that first commences, in its entirety: 1. During the “policy period” identified in Item 2.a. of the Declarations to this Policy; or, 2. If prior to the “policy period\" identified in Item 2.a. of the Declarations to this Policy, on or after the on or after the Retroactive Date, if any, identified on this Endorsement above."
  },
  {
    "id": "c185",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Limits of Liability",
    "text": "Limits of Liability The amount the Insurer shall pay pursuant to this Supplemental Coverage is subject to the Per Product Pollution Condition Sublimit of Liability and Aggregate Product Pollution Sublimit of Liability identified above. These Sublimits are included in, and not in addition to, the Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy. Therefore, this Aggregate Product Pollution Conditions Sublimit of Liability shall be the maximum amount the Insurer shall pay for all “claims”, “remediation costs” and associated “legal defense expense” arising out of or related to “product pollution\". However, under no circumstance shall the Insurer be liable to pay any amount in excess of the applicable Limits or Aggregate Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy."
  },
  {
    "id": "c186",
