    "text": "The law of some jurisdictions of the United States of America require that the Superintendent, Commissioner or Director of Insurance (or their successor in office) be designated as the company's agent for service of process. In these jurisdictions, the company designates the Director of Insurance as the company's true and lawful attorney upon whom service of process on the company's behalf may be made. The company also authorizes the Director of Insurance to mail process received on the company's behalf to the company person named above."
